{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "022A", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0003": "$T$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{U_j \\to T\\}_{j = 1, \\ldots, n}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0006": "$U_j$", "MATH_0007": "$U_j$", "MATH_0008": "$T_i$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-fpqc-affine}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f29f6d66fe0b484027fb4ce17473f56ae87f7e5f38fc7b5554d3c28e068afed8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9f59589b4bff9704a1bd20c17898c1661885c0d163550785a8e3fe1b0acfab4f", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an affine scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an fpqc covering of <MATH_0003>.\nThen there exists an fpqc covering\n<MATH_0004> which is a refinement\nof <MATH_0005> such that each <MATH_0006> is an affine\nscheme. Moreover, we may choose each <MATH_0007> to be open affine\nin one of the <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:76b6cd865cf25969c552764fdb353b14324d3b51ea95b9a8893076dd857dc441", "unit_id": "tag:022E:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "022A", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:600ea9a8d459244cb0fad3476d5f3bc66c20bc3be1c2c7f995a69270491e3471", "source_text": "This follows directly from the definition.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a36cab0888b22c7a799dc3f9c49578b10d76241c312afadaca68d4f01cfc6dad", "unit_id": "tag:022E:proof"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "022A", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$T$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{f_j : U_j \\to T\\}_{j = 1, \\ldots, n}$", "MATH_0004": "$U_j$", "MATH_0005": "$T$", "MATH_0006": "$T = \\bigcup f_j(U_j)$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-standard-fpqc}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d2b1068f352373d940a601cc4cba9447b0387bb23af6e0761c5d806cc42954fc", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1c52ee70a9f8f90d00d1fa141aa19bc37b73ed3ae48df1c2537e3804a8e58cbc", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an affine scheme. A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>standard fpqc covering<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nof <MATH_0002> is a family <MATH_0003>\nwith each <MATH_0004> is affine, flat over <MATH_0005> and <MATH_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:19f308edd4f22609a2be4f1fcb0d8547a213137c5e77eb0c848a2a7d4b3e7c35", "unit_id": "tag:022F:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "022A", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:315baabaf6438d1fe0feb8dbb1162300a5a83949413bec9bfd4714b7a1aa5518", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nSince we do not introduce the affine site we have to show directly\nthat the collection of all standard fpqc coverings satisfies the\naxioms.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:388d102a5188a602198bdf124c885e3dbcca06f5b18586790d0965bdffa6e1a5", "unit_id": "tag:022A:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "022A", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$T' \\to T$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{T' \\to T\\}$", "MATH_0004": "$T$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0006": "$i$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{T_{ij} \\to T_i\\}_{j\\in J_i}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\{T_{ij} \\to T\\}_{i \\in I, j\\in J_i}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0010": "$T' \\to T$", "MATH_0011": "$\\{T' \\times_T T_i \\to T'\\}_{i\\in I}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-fpqc-affine-axioms}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9e2cfe153eb45f4e05511defe14a0d0d67a3d5c22cf50aff12afe0aee9a4b79d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:257ec65fb497ab8de8509b407a63608720a2acd9a5331e2e3242850476c0d5d1", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an affine scheme.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> If <MATH_0002> is an isomorphism then <MATH_0003>\nis a standard fpqc covering of <MATH_0004>.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0005> is a standard fpqc covering and for each\n<MATH_0006> we have a standard fpqc covering <MATH_0007>, then\n<MATH_0008> is a standard fpqc covering.\n<STRUCT_0004> If <MATH_0009> is a standard fpqc covering\nand <MATH_0010> is a morphism of affine schemes then\n<MATH_0011> is a standard fpqc covering.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5d5409dc73292ee725ca92808e61ca6b9c2da3f01920b48fb8631a5058e5dd5b", "unit_id": "tag:03LA:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "022A", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-base-change-flat}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-composition-flat}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-fibre-product-affines}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a97e00ff3c54fa6cc52fff6f53f2e31ade13dfe6c2170c896b1f970b1ec2e333", "source_text": "This follows formally from the fact that compositions and base changes\nof flat morphisms are flat\n(Morphisms, Lemmas <REF_0001> and\n<REF_0002>)\nand that fibre products of affine schemes are affine\n(Schemes, Lemma <REF_0003>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ce93974c2b582c5dc205829ed8ca77e8dabc4bb9ebd10c63863ae8906d570cac", "unit_id": "tag:03LA:proof"}
